      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5fca5df4d58780532024a52b|full_name}: fair enough, quite a bit of RND would be needed to make a way to stream the render textures and stream player coordinates.\nand this could help quite alot of people as vrchat is full of demanding worlds and avatars and being able to be in a pc only world with your headset managing most the avatars on a quest only world but your pc gives you the better looking avatars. Granted yes this is alot of work but physics bones was alot and only benefit it has is pc players having more CPU in a mainly GPU bottlenecked game.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-12-26T17:10:38.901Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Let players free up their pc by haveing the headset render the world or the quest versions of avatars (or maby a version for split where transparency is allowed and it's slightly more lenient)\nThis frees lower end HW up and means that more people can dip their toes in vrc pc without fps issues\nPros:\nLess GPU usage on pc due to not rendering all avatars or the world\nSlightly less CPU usage pc side from the world or avatar draw calls\nCons:\nYou would need to make a streamer like Virtual desktop to stream the parts not rendered on headset\nYou would have to use debth buffer to calculate if an avatar needs to be drawn over or behind something",
